# Study03 grouped cloud planes

Created `/Game/RXSkySystem/Cubeless/Maps/L_RXSkySystem_CloudCards` as a copy of the current RX preview. The original `L_RXSkySystem_Cubeless` and its two comparison cards remain available. The copy replaces those comparison cards with eight independent `RX_Grouped_*` StaticMeshActors under `CloudCards/Grouped`.

The 28 active Study03 VDB controls were grouped by their current world-space bounds and overlap from the bake origin. Existing historical group names were not used as the only grouping criterion. Each group was rendered in isolation through the original native Volumetric Cloud density material; members of one group therefore retain their combined density and internal shadowing. Other groups do not cast baked shadows into that group's texture.

| Plane | Source slots | Intent |
| --- | --- | --- |
| EastTower | 7,14,15,16,0,4,10 | Main eastern tower and adjoining bank |
| NorthEastBank | 23,24,25,6,27 | Northeastern bank and associated upper forms |
| NorthBank | 9,2,18 | Connected northern low bank |
| WestTower | 8,3,17,19 | Western tower and adjoining lobes |
| SouthWestSmall | 1 | Separate small southwestern cloud |
| SouthBank | 11,12,13,5 | Southern bank |
| UpperBank | 20,21,22 | Connected upper cloud mass |
| HighWisp | 26 | Separate high wisp |

Assets are under `/Game/RXSkySystem/CloudCards/Study03Grouped`. `package.json` preserves the source actors, transforms, sources and group projection. Baking helper materials are under `/Game/RXSkySystem/Baking/CloudCards/Study03Grouped`.

Each group uses two linear HDR 1024-square textures: Positive RGB = local +X/+Y at 20 degrees and +Z; Positive A = coverage. Negative RGB = local -X/-Y at 20 degrees and -Z; Negative A = mean of four horizontal transport captures. Each of eleven passes averages eight actual captures, sequentially (704 captures total). Coverage is explicitly rendered as extinction emission: the native VC scene capture alpha remains 1 and must not be treated as coverage. Source actor mip/density values are preserved. The quality profile uses the existing bounded Cubeless SVT capture settings; this is not a higher-resolution VDB reconstruction.

The plane mesh lies in local YZ and faces the bake origin, with local +X forward, +Y right and +Z up. Projection FOV and distance match each group's bounding volume; actor translation, rotation and scale are independently editable. Very wide groups remain a fixed-view approximation and have lower central angular texel density than narrow groups. Large viewpoint changes reveal the planar nature. Six-direction light response uses the plane's local frame and the RX environment collection. No VDB, MCP or authoring component is needed to render the finished planes.

In the copied RX actor, `CloudDome.Visible` is false; SkyDome remains visible. Construction Script and time changes preserve the visibility override. `EnableGodRays` remains false following the fog fix. The existing shared Blueprint is not changed. Original source layout poses were checked unchanged after capture; temporary lights/camera were destroyed, source material, active state, lighting and capture CVars restored.

Verified native material compilation, all eight nonempty coverage outputs, four surrounding views, sunset 17.8 and night 22.0. Restored the copied level's time 15.744. This is an initial grouping for artistic review, not a claim that every connected silhouette must remain grouped permanently. Evidence: `MCPGameProject/Saved/RXGroupedCloudCards`.

Final validation: full offline profile passed (42/42); recursive dependency audit of the eight card materials and owned mesh checked 36 packages with no MCP or VDB/CloudAuthoring references. Saved the new map and left it open at the central review origin. Runtime packaging and large player-camera movement were not tested.

## Daytime whiteout correction

The inherited dome grading flattened the grouped cards at high sun. Adjusted all eight material instances: MultipleScatteringStrength 0.35, DetailContrast 1.2, AmbientWrap 0.2, IllustrationSoftness 0, PaintPalette 0, PaintMass 0.15, DayMidtoneSkyBlend 0.35, ShadeRemapStrength 0, ShadeSkyInfluence 0, CloudColorIntensity 0.8. This bypasses the inherited curve remap and restores internal shading without rebaking or changing sky brightness, opacity or placement. Saved the eight instances. Reviewed the unchanged camera at the user's 15.36, then 10.0, 17.8 and 22.0; restored 15.36. Evidence: brightness_before.json and brightness_*.png in the existing evidence folder. Scalar-only changes add no dependencies or shader code; previous offline validation remains applicable.
